-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2018-1-5 — תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת (16.1.2018)
-- The Wage Controller updates the monthly childcare supplement (parental
-- rights) for a child up to age 5, under clause 11 of the framework
-- agreement of 12.1.2011, from 1.1.2018, and prints the new amounts.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 The letterhead (Wage and Labour Agreements, the Ministry of Finance's address), the date (16.1.2018), the circular's number, the addressee (the senior deputy to the Accountant-General) and the subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p8 The reference line "חוזרנו - הע-2017-1-2": the previous update, whose amounts this one replaces from 1.1.2018; no rule of its own.

@desc A child for whom the childcare supplement is claimed, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `child for the childcare supplement` HAS
    `up to age 5`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc the child is "עד גיל 5", the age the circular names; who that is, and who may claim, is clause 11 of the framework agreement of 12.1.2011, which this circular does not restate
    `place among the children`      IS A NUMBER  @desc 1 for "ילד אחד / ילד ראשון" (an only or first child), 2 for "ילד שני" (a second child), counted as clause 11 of the framework agreement counts them

§§ `The update`

-- The date the update takes effect, as printed ("החל מיום"). The amounts
-- below run from it until the next update replaces them, which this
-- circular does not date.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
`the update takes effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2018

-- "עפ"י הקבוע בסעיף 11 להסכם המסגרת": the update is made under clause 11 of
-- the framework agreement, whose method this circular does not restate;
-- it prints no index change, only the resulting amounts below, and those
-- are what it sets.

§§ `1–2 The amounts`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for an only or first child` IS 313

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for a second child` IS 211

-- The circular prints amounts for an only or first child and for a second
-- child, and nothing for any other: whether a third child is paid for is
-- the framework agreement's question, not this circular's, so this circular
-- gives NOTHING there rather than a zero it does not print.
@export default The monthly childcare supplement (in shekels) this update sets for a child, from the date it takes effect
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement` @desc the child
      `month` IS A DATE                                @desc a day in the month the supplement is for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month` IS
    BRANCH IF `month` LESS THAN `the update takes effect` THEN NOTHING
           IF (NOT c's `up to age 5`)                    THEN NOTHING
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 1   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for an only or first child`
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 2   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for a second child`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Payment`

DECLARE `childcare supplement action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the childcare supplement` HAS `childcare amount paid` IS A NUMBER

-- The update is for the employers that pay the supplement: from the date it
-- takes effect they pay it at the updated amount. The circular sets a
-- monthly amount ("לחודש") and no payment date; time here is counted in
-- months from the start of the month the supplement is for, and the
-- supplement is read as due within that month.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement`
      `month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `childcare supplement action`
DECIDE `the employer pays the updated supplement` c `month` IS
    CONSIDER `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month`
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        PARTY `the employer`
        MUST  `pay the childcare supplement` paid
              PROVIDED paid AT LEAST due
        WITHIN 1
        LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the childcare supplement was not paid at the updated amount for the month"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (Eran Yaakov, Wage Controller), the copy to the Civil Service Commissioner, the circular's serial (2018-10) and the department's address; no rule.

§§ `Examples`

`an only child of three` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 1

`a second child of two` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 2

`a third child of one` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 3

`a first child of seven` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS FALSE
        `place among the children` IS 1

#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 1 1 2018) EQUALS JUST 313
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a second child of two` (Date 15 3 2018) EQUALS JUST 211
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 31 12 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a third child of one` (Date 1 2 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a first child of seven` (Date 1 2 2018) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Paid in full within the month, the obligation is fulfilled; paid short,
-- it is still owed.
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 1 2 2018) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 313 AT 0
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 1 2 2018) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 263 AT 0

§§ `Property checks`

-- The update over its whole finite space: a child up to 5 or not, at
-- places 0 to 4 among the children, on the day before the update takes
-- effect, on that day and on the last day of its year.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE

`the days checked` MEANS
    LIST Date (Day `the update takes effect` MINUS 1),
         `the update takes effect`,
         Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR `the update takes effect`)

-- An amount is given exactly for a child up to 5 who is an only, first or
-- second child, from the day the update takes effect and not the day
-- before: no child the update prints an amount for is left without one,
-- and none it prints nothing for is given one.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN u YIELD
                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                        all (GIVEN d YIELD
                                isJust (`the monthly childcare supplement under this update` (`child for the childcare supplement` WITH `up to age 5` IS u, `place among the children` IS p) d)
                                EQUALS (u AND (p EQUALS 1 OR p EQUALS 2) AND d AT LEAST `the update takes effect`))
                            `the days checked`)
                    (range 0 4))
            `both booleans`

-- The two printed amounts: both positive, and the second child's below
-- the first's, as in the base circular's 300 and 200.
`both amounts are positive and the second is the smaller` MEANS
        `the monthly amount for a second child` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the monthly amount for a second child` LESS THAN `the monthly amount for an only or first child`
#ASSERT `both amounts are positive and the second is the smaller`

-- The amounts in force before this update, as circular 2017-1-2 prints them
-- (corpus circulars-sachar/2017-01_sachar_2017-1-2_maonot, ¶¶1–2). They are used here only to
-- check the printed amounts, never as a rule of this circular.
`the amount in force for an only or first child` MEANS 312
`the amount in force for a second child`         MEANS 210

-- This circular prints the new amounts and no index change. The base
-- circular's item ו updates the supplement once a year by one method, so
-- one change moves both amounts: some single factor, applied to both
-- amounts in force, gives both printed amounts at the printed step
-- (a whole shekel). Each printed amount allows a range of factors; the ranges
-- overlap.
`half the printed step` MEANS 0.5

GIVEN `before` IS A NUMBER, `after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the lowest factor that prints` `before` `after` IS
    (`after` MINUS `half the printed step`) DIVIDED BY `before`

GIVEN `before` IS A NUMBER, `after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the highest factor that prints` `before` `after` IS
    (`after` PLUS `half the printed step`) DIVIDED BY `before`

`one change moves both amounts` MEANS
    max (`the lowest factor that prints` `the amount in force for an only or first child` `the monthly amount for an only or first child`)
        (`the lowest factor that prints` `the amount in force for a second child` `the monthly amount for a second child`)
    AT MOST
    min (`the highest factor that prints` `the amount in force for an only or first child` `the monthly amount for an only or first child`)
        (`the highest factor that prints` `the amount in force for a second child` `the monthly amount for a second child`)
#ASSERT `one change moves both amounts`
